# Vantage — environment variables
#
# Every variable the app and its functions read, as of 2026-09-30.
# Names only. Never commit a real value.
#
# Two places, never mixed up:
#   · CLIENT (`VITE_*`): bundled into public JavaScript at build time.
#     Public values only. Set in `.env.local` (gitignored) for local
#     dev, and in the Netlify dashboard for deploys.
#   · SERVER (everything else): Netlify dashboard → Site configuration
#     → Environment variables, scoped to Functions. Never prefix one of
#     these with VITE_ — that publishes it.
#
# "If missing" says what happens when the variable is unset:
#   fails CLOSED — the feature refuses (401/403/500); nothing unsafe
#   fails OPEN   — the check it powers is skipped
#   fails SOFT   — the feature degrades or falls back and keeps working
#
# Adding a VITE_* var? Also add it to SECRETS_SCAN_OMIT_KEYS in
# netlify.toml, or Netlify's secrets scanner blocks the deploy when it
# finds the (intentionally public) value in dist/.
#
# To regenerate the list:
#   grep -rhoE "process\.env\.[A-Z0-9_]+|env\.[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+" netlify
#   grep -rhoE "import\.meta\.env\.[A-Z0-9_]+" src

# ═══ CLIENT — public, bundled ════════════════════════════════════════

# Supabase project URL and publishable (anon) key. RLS gates every table.
# REQUIRED. If missing: fails CLOSED — the app shows the boot error screen.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# RevenueCat PUBLIC SDK keys, per platform (native builds only).
# If missing: fails SOFT — purchases unavailable, the app stays on free.
VITE_REVENUECAT_API_KEY_IOS=
VITE_REVENUECAT_API_KEY_ANDROID=

# Origin the NATIVE shell calls functions on (apiUrl()/authFetch). The web
# build uses its own origin and ignores this.
# If missing: fails SOFT — defaults to the production site URL.
VITE_API_BASE=

# "true" in native builds (`npm run cap:*` sets it). Compiles owner-only
# surfaces and the trading widget OUT of the binary.
# If missing: web build — owner surfaces are compiled in (behind the UI gate).
VITE_NATIVE_BUILD=

# LEGACY. No longer read by the client (the owner check moved server-side);
# still read by some functions as a fallback for OWNER_EMAIL, below.
# VITE_OWNER_EMAIL=

# ═══ SERVER — Netlify functions only ═════════════════════════════════

# ── Supabase ──
# SUPABASE_URL               Project URL (same value as VITE_SUPABASE_URL).
#                            A few functions fall back to VITE_SUPABASE_URL;
#                            most do not.
#                            Missing: fails CLOSED — 500 "not configured".
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  Service role: bypasses RLS. THE secret.
#                            Missing: fails CLOSED — 500 "not configured";
#                            health.js reports 503.
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY          apikey for verifying user JWTs (requireUser,
#                            client-error, trading-summary). Falls back to
#                            VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, then the service key.
#                            Missing: fails SOFT.

# ── Owner / admin ──
# OWNER_EMAIL                Comma-separated. Server-side owner check for
#                            admin-set-rating, trading-summary, groups admin,
#                            recipe-from-video, moderation, ai-coach-daily
#                            (owner bypass of the Pro check). Falls back to
#                            VITE_OWNER_EMAIL. Missing: fails CLOSED —
#                            nobody is the owner.

# ── Scheduled functions ──
# CRON_SECRET                Manual (HTTP) trigger for snapshot-ratings,
#                            whoop-cron, oura-cron, settle-leagues, sent as
#                            X-Cron-Secret. Scheduled runs don't need it.
#                            Missing: fails CLOSED — HTTP triggering refused.
# PUSH_DISPATCH_SECRET       Same, for push-dispatch (X-Dispatch-Secret).
#                            Missing: fails CLOSED.

# ── AI ──
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY          ai-coach-daily, ai-food-detect, recipe-from-video,
#                            and group-crest image screening. Missing: fails
#                            SOFT — AI features return an error, and new
#                            crests wait as "pending" for manual review.
#                            Also set a monthly spend limit in the console.

# ── Push (FCM) ──
# FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON   Service-account JSON for FCM HTTP v1.
# FCM_PROJECT_ID             Firebase project id.
#                            Missing either: fails SOFT — push-dispatch
#                            sends nothing and marks queued rows attempted.

# ── Wearables (OAuth) ──
# WHOOP_CLIENT_ID            developer.whoop.com app.
# WHOOP_CLIENT_SECRET        Same; also the fallback OAuth-state HMAC key.
# OURA_CLIENT_ID             cloud.ouraring.com/oauth/applications.
# OURA_CLIENT_SECRET         Same; also the fallback OAuth-state HMAC key.
#                            Missing: fails CLOSED for that provider —
#                            connect/sync/cron refuse; nothing else affected.
# OAUTH_STATE_SECRET         Dedicated HMAC key for the OAuth `state`
#                            parameter. Missing: fails SOFT — falls back to
#                            the provider's client secret (rotate that and
#                            in-flight connects fail once).
# OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE        Origin registered with WHOOP/Oura as the redirect
#                            base, when it isn't the site's primary URL.
#                            Missing: fails SOFT — uses URL (below), then the
#                            request host.

# ── Billing (RevenueCat) ──
# REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_AUTH    Shared Authorization header value for the
#                            webhook (≥32 random chars; same value in RC →
#                            Integrations → Webhooks). Missing: fails CLOSED
#                            — every webhook is rejected.
# REVENUECAT_SECRET_API_KEY  REST secret. The webhook reads the subscriber's
#                            current state from RC instead of trusting event
#                            order; delete-account removes the RC subscriber.
#                            Missing: fails SOFT — webhook falls back to event
#                            logic; deletion skips the RC side (logged).
# REVENUECAT_ALLOW_SANDBOX   "true" lets SANDBOX (TestFlight) events change
#                            tiers. Missing: sandbox events are ignored —
#                            the safe production default.

# ── Widgets and food search ──
# FINNHUB_API_KEY            Market widget (free tier = 15-min DELAYED
#                            quotes, which the widget labels). Missing:
#                            fails SOFT — widget shows unavailable.
# GNEWS_API_KEY              News widget (headline + link only — never render
#                            article bodies). Missing: fails SOFT.
# FDC_API_KEY                USDA FoodData Central in food-search.
#                            Missing: fails SOFT — that source is skipped.
# FATSECRET_CLIENT_ID        FatSecret (restaurant menus) in food-search.
# FATSECRET_CLIENT_SECRET    Missing either: fails SOFT — source skipped.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY            recipe-from-video reads YouTube descriptions via
#                            the Data API. Missing: fails SOFT — falls back to
#                            reading the public watch page.

# ── Trading (owner-only, web-only) ──
# TRADING_REPORT_URL         Sibling app's read-only report endpoint.
# TRADING_REPORT_TOKEN       Read-only token, sent as an X-Vantage-Token
#                            header. SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Missing either:
#                            fails SOFT — the widget shows not configured.

# ── Provided by Netlify (do not set) ──
# URL                        The site's primary URL; default OAuth redirect base.

# ── Not configuration ──
# MODE / PROD                Vite built-ins (import.meta.env), not variables.
# TZ                         Set only by src/utils/helpers.test.mjs.
